    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0261" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/804: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-14T18:00:00-04:00">July 14, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. From Braden. La Paz’ 39, July 14, 1 p.m. Baldivieso here. Has not yet
                    received official offer portfolio of Foreign Affairs but will probably accept
                    though not sure whether by telegraph or after discussion in La Paz with Busch.
                    He is well-informed on the Chaco, believes best chance for a settlement is
                    through direct negotiations rather than arbitration, and will discuss matter
                    thoroughly with us before leaving for La Paz next Wednesday. My impression is
                    that he should be an improvement over Finot. Alvéstegui<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d260-f1"/> has received <pb facs="0262" n="252" xml:id="pg252"/>
                    cable from Busch reiterating complete confidence and requesting that he remain
                    as president of Bolivian delegation. Alvéstegui has accepted. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="4" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>David Alvéstegui, Chairman of the Bolivian delegation to the Chaco Peace
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
